TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/19422","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/19422","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/19422.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/19422.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-03T16:47:36Z"},"body":"Fixes #11368 (apparently canonical). \r\nFixes #10910. \r\nFixes #12107. \r\nFixes #13841.\r\nFixes #15186. \r\nFixes #15454. \r\nFixes #19418.\r\n\r\n`mypy` now understands attribute access on enum members - the \"recursive\" behaviour of supporting access of almost-all enum members from members. \"Almost\", because `.name` and `.value` take precedence even if a member of the same name exists.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom enum import Enum\r\n\r\nclass E(Enum):\r\n    FOO = 1\r\n    BAR = 1\r\n\r\n# The following is still a `E.BAR` instance:\r\nE.FOO.FOO.BAR.BAR\r\n```\r\n\r\nLooks like this is a much wanted feature.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/19422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/19422/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":18958360590,"node_id":"CE_lADOAGuhRc5lIzVfzwAAAARqAaAO","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/18958360590","actor":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followe